---
/**
 * about.astro — Architecture disclosure / colophon-style About page.
 *
 * Sections:
 *   1. What this is — editorial explanation of the publication + architecture
 *   2. How the voices work — knowledge graph description, plain language
 *   3. Why editorial, not app — deliberate publication-over-product framing
 *   4. About the architecture — agency link + attribution
 *
 * Copy must pass check-copy.sh (no forbidden phrases from POSITIONING.md).
 * Layout: BaseLayout region="neutral", readable container (680px max), vertical rhythm.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import RuleLine from '../components/atlas/RuleLine.astro';
import CoordinateStrip from '../components/atlas/CoordinateStrip.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — The Regional Table"
  description="The Regional Table is a working instance of a specialized expert persona architecture. Five regional cuisine experts, five knowledge graphs, one editorial publication."
  region="neutral"
>
  <div class="about-page container readable">

    <CoordinateStrip lat={0} lon={0} regionName="ABOUT" />

    <!-- Section 1 — What this is -->
    <section class="about-section">
      <h1 class="about-h1">
        The Regional Table is a working instance of a specialized expert persona architecture.
      </h1>

      <p class="about-body">
        Five regional cuisine experts each carry a voice, a knowledge graph, and an opinion.
        The site lets you browse recipes anchored to place and consult each expert directly.
        It is also a demonstration &mdash; the same pattern underlies the agency&rsquo;s work
        on Football-AI and other specialized-expert products built for clients who need a voice
        that knows something specific, deeply, and refuses to pretend otherwise.
      </p>

      <p class="about-body">
        The five regions are Naples (Neapolitan), Lyon (Lyonnais), New Orleans (Cajun &amp; Creole),
        New York City (Street Food), and Japan (Washoku). Each has one expert voice. Each voice
        has strong opinions about what you are doing wrong.
      </p>
    </section>

    <RuleLine weight="hair" />

    <!-- Section 2 — How the voices work -->
    <section class="about-section">
      <h2 class="about-h2">How the voices work</h2>

      <p class="about-body">
        Each region holds a knowledge graph of techniques, rivalries, integrity lines, sacred
        ingredients, and seasonal awareness. When you ask the Nonna about rag&ugrave;, she pulls
        from the Neapolitan graph &mdash; not a generic recipe database. She knows that rag&ugrave;
        napoletano is a Sunday dish that begins at 6am and takes eight hours minimum. She knows
        you cannot rush it. She knows the difference between a San Marzano DOP and an ordinary
        tinned tomato, and she will tell you.
      </p>

      <p class="about-body">
        The knowledge graph includes what the chef considers an integrity line: a rule where
        crossing it is not a matter of preference but of kind. The Washoku Shokunin does not
        allow kombu to boil &mdash; he will say so, plainly, and explain why. These lines come
        from the region&rsquo;s own culinary tradition, not from a general cooking style guide.
      </p>

      <p class="about-body">
        The chat is backed by Claude Haiku 4.5 with a persona-bridge layer. The persona bridge
        injects the region&rsquo;s knowledge graph and voice profile into each request. No
        buzzwords &mdash; just a system prompt that says: you are this person, this is what you
        know, this is what you will not compromise on.
      </p>
    </section>

    <RuleLine weight="hair" />

    <!-- Section 3 — Why editorial, not app -->
    <section class="about-section">
      <h2 class="about-h2">Why editorial, not app</h2>

      <p class="about-body">
        The decision to build The Regional Table as an editorial publication rather than a
        recipe-app interface was deliberate. An app asks you to search. A publication asks you
        to read. Those are different relationships to knowledge.
      </p>

      <p class="about-body">
        A recipe-app UI optimises for speed of access &mdash; find the dish, get the steps,
        close the app. That is fine for a different kind of product. This one is interested in
        something else: the opinion behind the recipe. Why the Lyonnais chef will not accept
        industrial stock. Why the Cajun grandmother measures the roux by smell and color, not
        by minutes. Why the NYC street food veteran has strong feelings about the fold of a
        slice. These are not search results. They are voices.
      </p>

      <p class="about-body">
        Editorial design &mdash; the hairline rules, the coordinate strips, the serif typography,
        the atlas grid &mdash; signals to the reader that this is a publication with a point of
        view, not a utility. The design earns the voice. The voice earns the trust.
      </p>
    </section>

    <RuleLine weight="hair" />

    <!-- Section 4 — About the architecture -->
    <section class="about-section">
      <h2 class="about-h2">About the architecture</h2>

      <p class="about-body">
        The Regional Table is built and maintained by
        <a href="https://verbalogix.com" class="about-link" rel="noopener">Verbalogix</a>,
        a web and AI agency. The specialized expert persona pattern demonstrated here is available
        as a foundation for client projects &mdash; sports analytics, professional trades,
        domain-specific advisory, and other areas where a generic AI voice is the wrong voice.
      </p>

      <p class="about-body about-attribution">
        Architecture by Eyal Nof. Voices researched and authored by the editorial team.
      </p>
    </section>

    <RuleLine weight="strong" />

    <nav class="about-nav" aria-label="Site navigation">
      <a href="/" class="about-nav__link caps">Cover</a>
      <span class="about-nav__sep" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
      <a href="/regions/" class="about-nav__link caps">Regions</a>
      <span class="about-nav__sep" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
      <a href="/recipes/" class="about-nav__link caps">Recipes</a>
      <span class="about-nav__sep" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
      <a href="/ask" class="about-nav__link caps">Ask the Master Chef</a>
      <span class="about-nav__sep" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
      <a href="/colophon" class="about-nav__link caps">Colophon</a>
    </nav>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    padding-block: var(--space-7) var(--space-10);
  }
  .readable {
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .about-section {
    padding-block: var(--space-7) var(--space-5);
  }

  .about-h1 {
    font-family: var(--ff-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 3.5vw, 2rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--fg);
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .about-h2 {
    font-family: var(--ff-sans);
    font-size: var(--fs-caps);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-caps);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--rule-strong);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-5);
  }

  .about-body {
    font-family: var(--ff-serif);
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
    line-height: var(--lh-body);
    color: var(--fg);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-5);
  }
  .about-body:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .about-attribution {
    color: var(--rule-strong);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .about-link {
    color: var(--fg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-faint);
    text-decoration: none;
    padding-bottom: 1px;
    transition: color 150ms ease, border-color 150ms ease;
  }
  .about-link:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .about-nav {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    padding-block: var(--space-5);
  }
  .about-nav__link {
    font-size: var(--fs-caps);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-caps);
    color: var(--rule-strong);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color 150ms ease;
  }
  .about-nav__link:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  .about-nav__sep { color: var(--rule); }
</style>
